    "Customer orders" : {},
    "A villager has ordered a potion. The flask with the paper ticket must end full of the potion shown on it." : {},
    "Then sort the rest" : {},
    "The recipe is done when every order is filled and every other flask holds one potion or nothing. The card above the board ticks each order off." : {},
    "Layered recipes" : {},
    "This ticket shows layers, bottom to top. Its flask must end with exactly that pattern." : {},
    "Keep the bottom" : {},
    "A potion only pours onto the same potion, so keep the bottom layers that match and top them up. Gather the rest of each potion in one flask." : {},
    "New: customer orders" : {},
    "New: layered recipes" : {},
    "order flask, wanted: %@" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver: a customer's order flask; the argument says what it must end with"
    },
    "order filled" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver: an order flask holds what was asked for"
    },
    "New reward: %@" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver announcement when rewards unlock"
    },
    "Apprentice" : {
      "comment" : "Story speaker name"
    },
    "Alchemist" : {
      "comment" : "Story speaker name"
    },
    "Welcome to my cellar, young one. Every great alchemist starts down here, among the dusty flasks." : {
      "comment" : "Story, chapter 1 (Apprentice Cellar)"
    },
    "It's all mixed up! Is that three different potions in one flask?" : {
      "comment" : "Story, chapter 1 (Apprentice Cellar)"
    },
    "Pour onto a matching potion or into an empty flask. One potion per flask, and we'll have order by supper." : {
      "comment" : "Story, chapter 1 (Apprentice Cellar)"
    },
    "Sorting potions. I can do that!" : {
      "comment" : "Story, chapter 1 (Apprentice Cellar)"
    },
    "This vault hasn't been opened in a hundred years. And these flasks are sealed shut!" : {
      "comment" : "Story, chapter 2 (Rune Vault)"
    },
    "Rune seals. Somewhere in the other flasks lies a rune-stone key of the same metal. Pour it onto its seal and the lock gives way." : {
      "comment" : "Story, chapter 2 (Rune Vault)"
    },
    "A treasure hunt inside a puzzle. Best day ever." : {
      "comment" : "Story, chapter 2 (Rune Vault)"
    },
    "Mind your step. The marsh mist creeps into the flasks and clouds whatever lies beneath." : {
      "comment" : "Story, chapter 3 (Misty Marsh)"
    },
    "So I can't see what's at the bottom?" : {
      "comment" : "Story, chapter 3 (Misty Marsh)"
    },
    "Not until you pour off what's on top. A good alchemist is patient, and a little curious." : {
      "comment" : "Story, chapter 3 (Misty Marsh)"
    },
    "So many books! Wait, that flask has a glowing rune on it." : {
      "comment" : "Story, chapter 4 (Glyph Library)"
    },
    "An essence flask. It takes only the potion its rune names, and politely refuses everything else." : {
      "comment" : "Story, chapter 4 (Glyph Library)"
    },
    "Politely?" : {
      "comment" : "Story, chapter 4 (Glyph Library)"
    },
    "It glares a little. Plan ahead and it will be your best helper." : {
      "comment" : "Story, chapter 4 (Glyph Library)"
    },
    "The Glass Works! My old friend the glassblower makes the finest flasks in the land." : {
      "comment" : "Story, chapter 5 (Glass Works)"
    },
    "Some of them look funny. That one has a skinny neck, and that one has a tap on its side!" : {
      "comment" : "Story, chapter 5 (Glass Works)"
    },
    "A narrow neck lets one layer through at a time, a funnel only takes potions in, and a tap pours from the bottom. Each one changes how the potions flow." : {
      "comment" : "Story, chapter 5 (Glass Works)"
    },
    "Brr! My potions froze solid on the way up the mountain." : {
      "comment" : "Story, chapter 6 (Frost Peak)"
    },
    "Frozen layers can't be poured. But watch the little numbers on the ice: every pour you make brings the thaw closer." : {
      "comment" : "Story, chapter 6 (Frost Peak)"
    },
    "So I keep brewing and they melt on their own. Cold hands, warm heart!" : {
      "comment" : "Story, chapter 6 (Frost Peak)"
    },
    "Careful now. The bog air makes some of the flasks bubble." : {
      "comment" : "Story, chapter 7 (Bubbling Bog)"
    },
    "What happens when they bubble?" : {
      "comment" : "Story, chapter 7 (Bubbling Bog)"
    },
    "Every few pours the bottom potion rises to the top. The little dial counts down to it." : {
      "comment" : "Story, chapter 7 (Bubbling Bog)"
    },
    "A flask that stirs itself? I like this bog." : {
      "comment" : "Story, chapter 7 (Bubbling Bog)"
    },
    "Why are these two flasks chained together?" : {
      "comment" : "Story, chapter 8 (Twin Towers)"
    },
    "Twins. Pour into one and the potion is shared evenly between both. And pour into a full flask with a brass pipe, and it pushes its bottom layer across." : {
      "comment" : "Story, chapter 8 (Twin Towers)"
    },
    "Chains, pipes… everything in these towers is connected!" : {
      "comment" : "Story, chapter 8 (Twin Towers)"
    },
    "Then think in pairs, and the towers will dance for you." : {
      "comment" : "Story, chapter 8 (Twin Towers)"
    },
    "My old hall, and my favorite cauldron. Here we don't just sort potions, we brew them." : {
      "comment" : "Story, chapter 9 (Alchemist's Hall)"
    },
    "The card under the cauldron shows two potions… and a new one?" : {
      "comment" : "Story, chapter 9 (Alchemist's Hall)"
    },
    "Pour one ingredient onto the other inside the cauldron and they become the potion on the card." : {
      "comment" : "Story, chapter 9 (Alchemist's Hall)"
    },
    "Real brewing at last!" : {
      "comment" : "Story, chapter 9 (Alchemist's Hall)"
    },
    "Is that… a dragon? Asleep on a mountain of gold?" : {
      "comment" : "Story, chapter 10 (Dragon's Hoard)"
    },
    "Shh. Its hoard is kept behind gates. Fill a switch flask to the top with one potion and its gate lifts." : {
      "comment" : "Story, chapter 10 (Dragon's Hoard)"
    },
    "And the dragon?" : {
      "comment" : "Story, chapter 10 (Dragon's Hoard)"
    },
    "Dragons love a tidy shelf. Let's not keep it waiting." : {
      "comment" : "Story, chapter 10 (Dragon's Hoard)"
    },
    "Every flask sorted, every gate open… and listen, the dragon is purring!" : {
      "comment" : "Story, ending"
    },
    "From a dusty cellar to a dragon's hoard. You're no apprentice any more, my friend." : {
      "comment" : "Story, ending"
    },
    "But… what happens now?" : {
      "comment" : "Story, ending"
    },
    "Now we put the kettle on. And tomorrow, there's always a new brew." : {
      "comment" : "Story, ending"
    },
